  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. Tamsin is not a spellcaster, so narration of her casting a spell is a divergence. Input 2 grants advantage because the cove is dark and her lantern is shuttered. Input 4 offers gold coins, but there is no currency in this game and Tamsin carries none: the expected call is null, and narration of coins changing hands is worth checking. Input 7 asks to swing a boathook that is not in state, to test PHANTOM detection; its expected call is null. Input 14 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Tamsin. Inputs 22 to 24 talk about the harbourmaster's deputy, who is not in state: narration that brings the deputy on stage is a phantom character. Input 19 leaves the lantern behind, so later narration of Tamsin carrying a lantern is a RESOURCE divergence. Inputs 5 to 13 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
